  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Why through ROS",
      "items": [
        "act() publishes on the contract topic and the bridge's own subscription forwards it: a passing setup test proves topic → bridge → WebSocket → page.",
        "open and camera have no topic, so they go straight to the phone (bridge_node.py 472–476)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Fixed: output tests with no phone",
      "items": [
        "Until d2b04ac an output test answered 204 with no phone connected, so the page looked as if it was sent (out() ignores server.send's result).",
        "act() now refuses it with \"no phone\" before publishing, and step 4 shows whether a phone is there (bridge_node.py 526–528). Robot programs' own messages are still dropped quietly."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Privacy",
      "items": [
        "The camera message carries ok, size, error, torch and decoded text only; frames stay in the phone's <video> element (face.js 530–601)."
      ]
    }
  ]
